The MIT licence below covers the source code of great-wiki. It does NOT cover the
typefaces bundled under web/static/fonts/, which are licensed separately.

    IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono    Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp.,
                                    with Reserved Font Name "Plex"
    Literata                        Copyright (c) 2017 The Literata Project Authors
    JetBrains Mono                  Copyright (c) 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors

Each is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, and each family's
OFL.txt sits beside its font files in web/static/fonts/<family>/. Condition 5 of the
OFL requires that these files remain entirely under the OFL: they are not relicensed
by being distributed here, and this MIT grant does not extend to them.

The maths faces are the exception, and are not OFL:

    KaTeX_*                         Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy
                                    and other contributors

They are KaTeX's own typefaces, copied unchanged from npm `katex`, and are under
KaTeX's MIT licence — a separate grant from this one, whose text sits beside them in
web/static/fonts/katex/LICENSE. See web/scripts/vendor-katex.mjs for how they got there.

IBM's licence reserves the name "Plex". Under the OFL, subsetting a font is
Modification, and a Modified Version may not use a Reserved Font Name. The IBM Plex
files here are therefore shipped exactly as IBM published them; see the note at the
top of web/src/lib/styles/fonts.css before touching them.

